{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793448927,"nonce":"kNEoyY9NNDra5v5ZD9wQJ8QRzsE=","title":"Lua typer: a value only tested for truth escapes","message":"`if`, `elseif`, `while` and `until` conditions and the operand of `not` go through `Round::value`, which escapes the value's type. A truthiness test hands the value to nobody (Lua takes truth raw, with no metamethod), yet `if not self.left then` in binary_trees marks the node shape as escaping, and with it the class behind its `__index` (Tree), so stores the types do not see are assumed to reach both. That keeps the method-lookup fold (376e906f) off every call in binary_trees and joins blind stores into the node's fields.\n\nFix: a condition context that walks `not`, `and`, `or` and parentheses without escaping; comparisons still escape their operands, which an `__eq`/`__lt`/`__le` handler receives.","files":null}]}